### 0. Obtain an access token from Keycloak (development client, password grant)
POST http://localhost:8180/realms/ecommerce/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=ecommerce-dev-cli&username=jane.doe@example.com&password=password

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token); %}

### 0b. Through the gateway: no token -> 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/carts/1

### 0c. Through the gateway with the token -> 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/carts/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 0d. Customer list is reserved to ADMIN -> 403 for Jane
GET http://localhost:8080/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 0e. Obtain an access token for the admin user
POST http://localhost:8180/realms/ecommerce/protocol/openid-connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=ecommerce-dev-cli&username=admin@example.com&password=password

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### 0f. Customer list with the admin token -> 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/customers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 0g. Internal endpoint, blocked at the gateway even for ADMIN -> 403
POST http://localhost:8080/api/inventory/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": 999, "items": [{"productId": "PRD-0001", "quantity": 1}]}

### End-to-end scenario, runnable from the IntelliJ HTTP client.
### Prerequisites: docker compose up -d, then the six services started with the "dev" profile (default).

### 1. Browse the catalog (seeded with PRD-0001 ... PRD-0005)
GET http://localhost:8083/api/products

### 2. Check the stock of a product
GET http://localhost:8084/api/inventory/PRD-0001

### 3. Create a customer
POST http://localhost:8085/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@example.com"
}

### 4. Add products to the cart of customer 1
POST http://localhost:8082/api/carts/1/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "PRD-0001",
  "quantity": 2
}

### 5. Add a second product
POST http://localhost:8082/api/carts/1/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "PRD-0004",
  "quantity": 1
}

### 6. Review the cart
GET http://localhost:8082/api/carts/1

### 7. Place the order
POST http://localhost:8081/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1
}

### 8. Order history of the customer
GET http://localhost:8081/api/orders?customerId=1

### 9. The cart has been emptied by the order.created event
GET http://localhost:8082/api/carts/1

### 10. Stock has been deducted (25 - 2 = 23)
GET http://localhost:8084/api/inventory/PRD-0001

### 11. Notifications sent (the e-mail itself is visible at http://localhost:8025)
GET http://localhost:8086/api/notifications?customerId=1

### 12. Out-of-stock scenario: expect 409 with unavailableProductIds
POST http://localhost:8082/api/carts/1/items
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "PRD-0003",
  "quantity": 50
}

###
POST http://localhost:8081/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1
}
